@startuml UpsertScopeBatch

title Upsert Scope Batch API Sequence

' Leading SQL apostrophes use &#39; so PlantUML preserves literals; parity compares decoded SQL.

' Visual style
skinparam defaultFontName "Sarabun"
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 10
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #475569
    ArrowFontColor #334155
    LifeLineBorderColor #CBD5E1
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    ParticipantBorderColor #94A3B8
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
    ParticipantFontColor #0F172A
    GroupBorderColor #94A3B8
    GroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
    GroupFontColor #334155
}

' Do not show participant footers at the bottom of the diagram
hide footbox

actor "User" as user
box "Frontend" #F8FAFC
    participant "Upsert Scope Batch Page" as page
end box
box "Web API" #F8FAFC
    participant "API" as api
    participant "Application" as app
    participant "Domain" as domain
    participant "Infrastructure" as infra
end box
box "Database" #F8FAFC
    database "m_user" as m_user
    database "t_user_access_token" as t_user_access_token
    database "m_scope" as m_scope
    database "t_permission_scope" as t_permission_scope
end box

user -> page: Submit the ordered scope batch
activate page
    page -> api: POST v1/author/scope/upsert/batch (JSON, Bearer JWT, UTC timestamp)
    activate api
        api -> app: [**UpsertScopeBatchCommandHandler**] Process request
        activate app
            note over app, infra
                Execution order: validate all items (400) -> verify JWT (401) -> begin transaction (READ COMMITTED) ->
                caller lock -> fresh current credential gate (401) -> lock target ids ascending -> all target existence
                checks in request order (404) -> one claims permission (403, E10009) -> per-item duplicate/in-use conflicts
                (409) and guarded writes in input order -> complete indexed mapping -> COMMIT -> one 200. Every post-BEGIN
                error rolls back the whole batch.
            end note
            app -> app: Generate requestId; validate whole JSON envelope/no query/known unique keys, UTC timestamp, scopes array 1..100, every item type/required fields/code/status/defaults; reject insert-DELETED
            note over app, infra
                Validate the whole request before SQL: exactly one JSON object with only scopes, no query keys, correct JSON
                content type and mandatory UTC timestamp; scopes is an array of 1..100 non-null objects with only
                id/scope/name/description/rowStatus and no repeated JSON keys. Process item validation in input order;
                required scope/name/description are non-null nonblank strings (max 64/64/256), scope matches
                ^[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{0,63}$, and values are not trimmed/case-normalized. id is optional only by omission;
                supplied id must be a non-null UUID. rowStatus defaults to ACTIVE only when omitted, otherwise
                ACTIVE/INACTIVE/DELETED/LOCKED/ARCHIVED; insert-DELETED is 400. Validate required fields even for
                delete/archive. Generate requestId if omitted.
            end note
            app -> app: Validate all items in input order; canonical duplicate ids and exact duplicate non-DELETED scope codes are 400 before SQL
            alt Invalid envelope/header/item/count/duplicate ids or scope codes
                break Reject this whole request
                    app -> api: HTTP 400 E10001 item errors use scopes[i]; request-level errors have no invented position
                    api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                    page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and structured unique roleIds/name array
            alt Missing/invalid JWT or malformed roles
                break Reject this whole request
                    app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                    api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                    page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                end break
            else Check passed
            end
            app -> app: callerUserId = verified sub; accessTokenHash = SHA-256 exact JWT; createdBy/updatedBy = caller UUID string
            app -> app: targetScopeIds = typed UUID[] of supplied canonical ids, empty for all inserts; omitted per-item id = typed SQL NULL
            app -> infra: BEGIN READ COMMITTED
            note over app, infra
                When any item fails the whole request is rolled back and no scope is changed. `id` must not be duplicated in
                the request, and `scope` must not be duplicated among the items that are not DELETED (400, E10001). An item
                without `id` and with `rowStatus` DELETED is rejected with 400 (E10001). The response is HTTP 200 for every
                successful batch, including a batch that deletes. The 403 message has no item position (the permission is
                the caller's, not the item's).
                Verify JWT signature/issuer/audience/expiry/UUID sub and structured roles before BEGIN. roles must be an
                array (including []), each object has UUID roleId and non-empty string name, and roleIds are unique;
                missing/malformed claims are generic 401 E10002, not an empty-role fallback. Derive callerUserId only from
                verified sub, accessTokenHash as SHA-256 of the exact JWT, createdBy/updatedBy as caller UUID string. Never
                use request flags or a separate isPlatformAdmin claim to grant permission.
                Begin one READ COMMITTED transaction, lock caller user first, capture fresh server UTC now after the lock
                and recheck JWT exp, then read joined current credential/user. Require matching hash/caller, ACTIVE
                token/user and strict expired_at > now. Missing caller or revoked/inactive/expired/mismatched credentials is
                generic 401 before target reads. Logout/reset use the same user-first lock. Withdrawal of a grant alone does
                not invalidate an otherwise-current old JWT role snapshot; refresh loads current grants.
                Construct targetScopeIds as a typed UUID[] of all supplied ids (empty array for all inserts). Lock every
                matching non-DELETED target scope in ascending id order with one SELECT FOR UPDATE, independent of request
                order, before any in-use check or write. Map locked rows by id, then report the first missing/DELETED target
                in original request order as scopes[i]: Scope not found. (404 E10004), before caller permission or any
                conflict/write. The row-lock query rechecks lifecycle after waiting; no resurrection. Request-order mutation
                and sorted lock order are separate concerns. Existing scopes cannot appear twice because validation rejects
                duplicate ids.
                Each item's conflict reads see preceding item writes in the same transaction. Deleting a scope at index 0
                can release its old code for an insert at index 1; reversing those items returns duplicate 409 at index 0
                and applies neither. Recoding A to a code still held by B returns 409 even if a later item would release it;
                this API does not apply a final-state recode plan. Preserve the existing request-order rule. Every
                item-specific 404/409 message begins scopes[i]; a unique-index collision uses the current writing item's
                index.
                Shared lifecycle invariant: lock order is caller user -> target scopes ascending by id -> usage
                reads/writes. Reference writers adding/retaining an ACTIVE permission-scope definition must lock/recheck
                their permission parents and then scope masters ordered by id before link mutation, as in the separately
                delivered permission APIs; this batch contract does not certify unmigrated writers. A soft master status is
                not protected by a foreign key alone. Q23 withdrawal only reduces usage and does not authorize creating a
                link to a closed master.
            end note
            activate infra
            alt Work completes before commit
                note over app, infra
                    Unique-index collision, timeout or unexpected failure may interrupt a SQL/domain step, including a later item.
                    All earlier writes are provisional until the one final COMMIT; any failure rolls back every item.
                end note
                app -> infra: QUERY - Lock the caller user
                infra -> m_user: QUERY - Lock the caller user
                activate m_user
                    note right of m_user
                        SELECT
                            u.id as user_id
                        FROM authen.m_user u
                        WHERE u.id = '<sequence.callerUserId>'
                        FOR UPDATE
                    end note
                    m_user -> infra: Return locked caller user or no row
                deactivate m_user
                infra -> app: Return locked caller user or no row
                alt Caller user is missing
                    break Reject this whole request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                        page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Capture fresh server UTC now after caller lock; recheck JWT exp
                alt JWT expired while waiting for caller lock
                    break Reject this whole request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                        page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                infra -> t_user_access_token: QUERY - Check current credential and user
                activate t_user_access_token
                    note right of t_user_access_token
                        SELECT
                            at.id as access_token_id
                        FROM authen.t_user_access_token at
                        JOIN authen.m_user u ON u.id = at.user_id
                        WHERE at.token = '<sequence.accessTokenHash>'
                        AND at.user_id = '<sequence.callerUserId>'
                        AND at.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                        AND at.expired_at > '<sequence.now>'
                        AND u.row_status = 'ACTIVE'
                    end note
                    t_user_access_token -> infra: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                deactivate t_user_access_token
                infra -> app: Return ACTIVE matching unexpired token/user or no row
                alt Current token/user missing/inactive/revoked/expired/mismatched
                    break Reject this whole request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 401 E10002 Invalid or expired access token.
                        api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                        page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> infra: QUERY - Lock existing scopes
                infra -> m_scope: QUERY - Lock existing scopes
                activate m_scope
                    note right of m_scope
                        SELECT
                            s.id as scope_id
                        FROM author.m_scope s
                        WHERE s.id = ANY ('<sequence.targetScopeIds>'::UUID[])
                        AND s.row_status <> 'DELETED' -- the id of a DELETED scope counts as not found
                        ORDER BY s.id
                        FOR UPDATE
                    end note
                    m_scope -> infra: Return all non-DELETED target scope_id rows locked in ascending id order
                deactivate m_scope
                infra -> app: Return all non-DELETED target scope_id rows locked in ascending id order
                app -> app: Map locked scopes by id; check all supplied target ids in original input order; choose first missing index i (empty target set is valid)
                alt Any supplied target id missing or DELETED after lock wait
                    break Reject this whole request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 scopes[i]: Scope not found.
                        api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                        page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                app -> app: Authorize once using only exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN in verified JWT roles; never reload live grants
                alt No exact PLATFORM_ADMIN role claim
                    break Reject this whole request
                        app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                        app -> api: HTTP 403 E10009 You do not have permission to manage scopes. (no item position)
                        api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                        page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                    end break
                else Check passed
                end
                loop For every scopes[i] in original request order; all writes remain provisional
                    app -> app: currentIndex = i; bind this item fields and server audit/now; prior item writes are visible
                    alt This item id omitted (INSERT, including ARCHIVED)
                        app -> infra: QUERY - Check duplicate scope
                        infra -> m_scope: QUERY - Check duplicate scope
                        activate m_scope
                            note right of m_scope
                                SELECT
                                    s.id as scope_id
                                FROM author.m_scope s
                                WHERE s.scope = '<sequence.scopes.scope>'
                                AND s.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                AND ('<sequence.scopes.id>' IS NULL OR s.id <> '<sequence.scopes.id>') -- omitted insert id is typed SQL NULL
                            end note
                            m_scope -> infra: Return same-code non-DELETED scope after preceding item writes, excluding optional current id
                        deactivate m_scope
                        infra -> app: Return same-code non-DELETED scope after preceding item writes, excluding optional current id
                        alt Another non-DELETED scope holds this scope code
                            break Reject this whole request
                                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 scopes[i]: Scope scope already exists.
                                api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                                page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                            end break
                        else Check passed
                        end
                        app -> infra: INSERT - Create scope
                        infra -> m_scope: INSERT - Create scope
                        activate m_scope
                            note right of m_scope
                                INSERT INTO author.m_scope (
                                    created_by,
                                    created_at,
                                    row_status,
                                    scope,
                                    name,
                                    description
                                )
                                VALUES (
                                    &#39;<sequence.createdBy>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.now>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.scopes.rowStatus>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.scopes.scope>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.scopes.name>',
                                    &#39;<sequence.scopes.description>'
                                )
                                RETURNING id as scope_id
                            end note
                            m_scope -> infra: Return inserted scope_id
                        deactivate m_scope
                        infra -> app: Return inserted scope_id
                        app -> app: Require exactly one inserted scope_id; missing/malformed result is internal failure; action = INSERT
                    else This item id supplied (UPDATE, DELETE or ARCHIVE)
                        app -> infra: QUERY - Check duplicate scope
                        infra -> m_scope: QUERY - Check duplicate scope
                        activate m_scope
                            note right of m_scope
                                SELECT
                                    s.id as scope_id
                                FROM author.m_scope s
                                WHERE s.scope = '<sequence.scopes.scope>'
                                AND s.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                AND ('<sequence.scopes.id>' IS NULL OR s.id <> '<sequence.scopes.id>') -- omitted insert id is typed SQL NULL
                            end note
                            m_scope -> infra: Return same-code non-DELETED scope after preceding item writes, excluding optional current id
                        deactivate m_scope
                        infra -> app: Return same-code non-DELETED scope after preceding item writes, excluding optional current id
                        alt Another non-DELETED scope holds this scope code
                            break Reject this whole request
                                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 scopes[i]: Scope scope already exists.
                                api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                                page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                            end break
                        else Check passed
                        end
                        alt Requested item rowStatus is DELETED or ARCHIVED
                            app -> infra: QUERY - Check permission scope in use
                            infra -> t_permission_scope: QUERY - Check permission scope in use
                            activate t_permission_scope
                                note right of t_permission_scope
                                    SELECT
                                        ps.id as permission_scope_id
                                    FROM author.t_permission_scope ps
                                    WHERE ps.scope_id = '<sequence.scopes.id>' -- only when rowStatus is DELETED or ARCHIVED
                                    AND ps.row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                end note
                                t_permission_scope -> infra: Return non-DELETED permission-scope definition or no row
                            deactivate t_permission_scope
                            infra -> app: Return non-DELETED permission-scope definition or no row
                            alt A non-DELETED permission-scope definition exists
                                break Reject this whole request
                                    app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                    app -> api: HTTP 409 E10006 scopes[i]: Scope is used by permissions.
                                    api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                                    page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                                end break
                            else Check passed
                            end
                        else Requested item rowStatus is ACTIVE, INACTIVE or LOCKED
                            app -> app: Preserve existing permission-scope definitions; no in-use rejection for this status
                        end
                        app -> infra: UPDATE - Update or delete scope
                        infra -> m_scope: UPDATE - Update or delete scope
                        activate m_scope
                            note right of m_scope
                                UPDATE author.m_scope
                                SET
                                    updated_by = '<sequence.updatedBy>',
                                    updated_at = '<sequence.now>',
                                    row_status = '<sequence.scopes.rowStatus>',
                                    scope = '<sequence.scopes.scope>',
                                    name = '<sequence.scopes.name>',
                                    description = '<sequence.scopes.description>'
                                WHERE id = '<sequence.scopes.id>'
                                AND row_status <> 'DELETED'
                                RETURNING id as scope_id
                            end note
                            m_scope -> infra: Return guarded returned scope_id or no row
                        deactivate m_scope
                        infra -> app: Return guarded returned scope_id or no row
                        alt Guarded UPDATE returned zero rows
                            break Reject this whole request
                                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                                app -> api: HTTP 404 E10004 scopes[i]: Scope not found.
                                api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                                page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
                            end break
                        else Check passed
                        end
                        app -> app: Require exactly one returned scope_id equal to this input id; mismatch is internal failure
                        app -> app: action = DELETE for DELETED, ARCHIVE for ARCHIVED, otherwise UPDATE
                    end
                    app -> app: Append exactly index=i, scopeId from RETURNING and action to ordered results; do not emit per-item HTTP
                end
                app -> app: Require results count equals input count, original index order and unique returned scopeIds; data = exactly scopes array of index/scopeId/action; map all before COMMIT
                app -> infra: COMMIT
                infra -> app: Return committed whole batch
                note over app, infra
                    This detailed revision remains in-review; no backend/schema implementation is included.
                    Every scope follows the rules of [the single upsert](../07-upsert-scope/spec.md#scope-rules): scope is the
                    scope code: capital letters, DELETED is final, delete and archive are rejected while a permission
                    (`author.t_permission_scope`) that is not DELETED still uses it.
                    Valid non-admin claims return one 403 E10009 after all target existence checks and before any conflict or
                    write, with no item position. Never reload live caller grants from author.t_user_role/author.m_role.
                    Approved by the product owner (Q2/Q4/Q10/Q13, 2026-11-07), superseding the earlier live-assignment guard.
                    Input errors identify scopes[i] where item-specific; count/envelope/header errors are request-level. No
                    partial processing before validation is complete.
                    After all target ids exist, authorize once using exact case-sensitive PLATFORM_ADMIN from verified JWT
                    roles. Empty roles or other valid roles is one 403 E10009 with no item index; skip all conflict/write work.
                    Do not query the caller's live assignments or reload claims, and do not infer authority from a scope code.
                    The usage read below protects the master lifecycle only.
                    Then iterate scopes[i] in original input order. Check duplicate scope codes with a null-safe optional target
                    exclusion, across all non-DELETED statuses; omitted insert id binds typed SQL NULL. For an existing locked
                    target requested DELETED/ARCHIVED, any non-DELETED permission-scope definition is 409 E10006, including
                    INACTIVE/LOCKED/ARCHIVED definitions and regardless of its parent permission's lifecycle; no
                    parent/master/grant JOIN or ACTIVE-only filter may hide usage. INACTIVE/LOCKED and ordinary metadata/code
                    updates leave definitions unchanged. Insert-ARCHIVED is INSERT and needs no usage check.
                    Bind every SQL value. INSERT explicitly sets created_at from fresh server now and must return exactly one
                    scope_id; zero/malformed result is internal 500. UPDATE guards target id and non-DELETED status; zero
                    returns scopes[i]: Scope not found. (404 E10004), no result or earlier mutation is committed. Exactly one
                    returned update id must equal that input id. Preserve creation audit on update; never trust a
                    client-generated inserted id or audit fields. Existing scope codes, including seed codes, remain editable
                    under the original contract; no reserved-code rule is added and no permission definition or grant history is
                    rewritten.
                    Append exactly index/scopeId/action per item, using RETURNING. index is its original zero-based position.
                    action is INSERT when id omitted (including insert-ARCHIVED), otherwise DELETE for DELETED, ARCHIVE for
                    ARCHIVED, UPDATE for ACTIVE/INACTIVE/LOCKED. All item outcomes, including DELETE, remain in data.scopes.
                    Require exactly one result per input item in the same order with no duplicate returned scopeIds. Finish all
                    mapping before one COMMIT after the loop, then HTTP 200 S10000 Batch Upsert Scope Success; batch never sends
                    per-item 201/204 or partial success.
                    uq_m_scope_scope is the final concurrent duplicate guard. SQLSTATE 23505 from that constraint rolls back all
                    items and returns 409 E10003 scopes[i]: Scope scope already exists.; other SQL/result/mapping failures roll
                    back and return generic 500 without bizCode. Timeout before COMMIT rolls back and returns 408 E90001. These
                    request-level failures have no invented item position. No success or partial result escapes a failed
                    transaction; no retry is promised after an unknown commit result.
                end note
                app -> api: HTTP 200 S10000 Batch Upsert Scope Success; all ordered scopes results including DELETE
                api -> page: Show all committed indexed actions
                page -> user: Display the entire saved batch
            else SQLSTATE 23505 from uq_m_scope_scope at currentIndex (concurrent collision)
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 409 E10003 scopes[i]: Scope scope already exists. (i = currentIndex)
                api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
            else Timeout before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 408 E90001
                api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
            else Unexpected SQL/result/mapping failure before COMMIT
                app -> infra: ROLLBACK
                app -> api: HTTP 500 Internal Server Error; omit bizCode
                api -> page: Reject the whole batch; no partial results
                page -> user: Display failure; no scope action is reported as successful
            end
            deactivate infra
        deactivate app
    deactivate api
deactivate page
@enduml
